Z||000010||sqoach||10-06-2001||07:09 PM||||Yes, next time I go up there I think I'll use sunscreen. Man, it hurts to drive my car, cuz my back is against the seat. It's even hard to sleep. When I'm laying down for a while, then bend one way or the other, it hurts too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>At least I'll be smart enough to not get burned again. A cold front moved through, so that's a relief. Only got up in the low 60's today  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>We <I>should</I> be finishing up before next weekend. We have half of the roof decked and tar-papered. Half of the front, I should say. We did the back a couple years ago. These are the times when you don't like a big house  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Thanks for the replies  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||maryjane||10-06-2001||09:34 PM||||You're welcome, Sqoach. Actually glad to hear some people still do their own house repairs. I work with Christmas In April, a do-gooder type thing, repairing homes of people who can't do it themselves or afford to have it done by a contractor. The last 2 years have both been roofs. Not just felt & shingles, the whole roof, joists, rafters, decking,everything. It was a killer, I know what you feel like. My back may never be the same again.||||reg||1
